# Postgres user's crontab — pgBackRest schedule (config-as-code; see
# docs/runbooks/database-backup-restore.md, §Tier 1 and bring-up step 8).
#
# This file is the canonical source: a rebuilt droplet gets its schedule
# from the repo, not from a human's memory of a runbook. Install/replace
# with:
#
#   sudo -u postgres crontab deploy/cron.d/priori-pgbackrest.cron
#
# WARNING: `crontab <file>` replaces the user's ENTIRE crontab — merge any
# new entries into this file (in the repo, via MR), never hand-edit on the
# droplet.
#
# The 00:30 slot finishes before the 01:15 nightly dump (deploy user's
# crontab, priori-backups.cron). pgBackRest writes its own logs to
# /var/log/pgbackrest; failures also surface through the CI freshness job.

# weekly full backup — Sunday 00:30 UTC
30 0 * * 0 pgbackrest --stanza=priori --type=full backup

# daily differential — Monday-Saturday 00:30 UTC
30 0 * * 1-6 pgbackrest --stanza=priori --type=diff backup

# daily self-check: config sane, archiving round-trip works, repo reachable
15 6 * * * pgbackrest --stanza=priori check

# weekly deep verification of repository checksums
45 6 * * 0 pgbackrest --stanza=priori verify
